# `milp::to_string`

The name of a mixed-integer `Status` as text.

## Signature

```cpp
const char *milp::to_string(milp::Status value);
```

## What It Does

`Result::status` is a `milp::Status`, an enumerator; `to_string` returns its name for reports and logs: `Optimal`, `Infeasible`, `Unbounded` or `NodeLimit`.

## Parameters

`milp::Status value`
: The status to name.

## Returns

A static name; `"Unknown"` for an invalid value.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

All four names.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace milp = pluss::subsp::math::milp;
namespace linprog = pluss::subsp::math::linprog;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  for (const milp::Status status : {milp::Status::Optimal, milp::Status::Infeasible, milp::Status::Unbounded, milp::Status::NodeLimit}) {
    out.writeln(static_cast<int>(status), "->", milp::to_string(status));
  }
}
```

### Example 2

Naming the verdict of a solve.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace milp = pluss::subsp::math::milp;
namespace linprog = pluss::subsp::math::linprog;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  // maximise 10a + 13b + 7c + 8d   subject to   3a + 4b + 2c + 3d <= 7,  each item taken or not
  milp::Problem problem;
  problem.lp.c = pluss::series::make({-10.0, -13.0, -7.0, -8.0});
  problem.lp.a_ub = pluss::series::make({{3.0, 4.0, 2.0, 3.0}});
  problem.lp.b_ub = pluss::series::make({7.0});
  problem.lp.lower = pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0});
  problem.lp.upper = pluss::series::make({1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0});
  problem.integer = pluss::series::make({1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0});

  out.writeln("verdict =", milp::to_string(milp::solve(problem).status));
}
```

### Example 3

In a report line together with the bound.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace milp = pluss::subsp::math::milp;
namespace linprog = pluss::subsp::math::linprog;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  // maximise 10a + 13b + 7c + 8d   subject to   3a + 4b + 2c + 3d <= 7,  each item taken or not
  milp::Problem problem;
  problem.lp.c = pluss::series::make({-10.0, -13.0, -7.0, -8.0});
  problem.lp.a_ub = pluss::series::make({{3.0, 4.0, 2.0, 3.0}});
  problem.lp.b_ub = pluss::series::make({7.0});
  problem.lp.lower = pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0});
  problem.lp.upper = pluss::series::make({1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0});
  problem.integer = pluss::series::make({1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0});

  milp::Options options;
  options.max_nodes = 1;
  const milp::Result result = milp::solve(problem, options);
  out.writeln("[", milp::to_string(result.status), "] bound =", result.best_bound);
}
```

